   "scope": "the finite core \u2014 the sum-of-squares SDP infeasible at lambda = 120 \u2014 is decided here by our own exact certificate; the step from that infeasibility to a PSD tuple violating the inequality is the noncommutative Positivstellensatz for bounded linear matrix-inequality domains (Helton--Klep--McCullough 2012, as Lai--Lim's Theorem 3 states it), a published theorem CITED and not re-derived, which the claimant's paper also declares external; the reduction from the inequality to the Loewner form and the equivalence with Bandeira's statement are read above; the Lean development certifies the claimant's certificate's arithmetic and not the SDP's infeasibility (row bandeira-02a-lean-reading), so nothing here rests on it. A claim whose analytic step rests on a cited theorem is certified with that step named, as the register does for Mathlib's theorems.",
